matrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2}$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-2{a}_{3}=0.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-2{a}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+1-2 \\\\ 2+0-2 \\\\ 0+2-2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false. Since statement ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-2{a}_{3}=0.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ for ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{3}=-2.$\n\n- Statement “The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly independent” is false. Since statement “${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” is false, the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${a}_{1}+{a}_{2}-2{a}_{3}=0.$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120293 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6d66bec-4f70-53d2-9ff4-2520b4c8cdf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117898} {:answer/id #uuid "f4d4957d-eb5a-5c29-b427-cd7789e9a7a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117899} {:answer/id #uuid "2eb48522-7684-5c49-9b22-80599f5f6575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117900} {:answer/id #uuid "55c5a60b-30f3-5dd0-8c86-12e610e70a02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117901} {:answer/id #uuid "5f15135e-67c9-596b-bf5d-2210d31c2fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6d66bec-4f70-53d2-9ff4-2520b4c8cdf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117898} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb5fae5b-0364-5098-baba-4caac87e9d00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b9323edd-e697-569c-8dd2-3fe5f9eed059" :question/math-academy-id "q-34054" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation we get ${x}_{2}=2$, which we substitute into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} & =3 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+2 & =3 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=2$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ -(-1)+2(2) & =5 \\\\ 5 & =5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=2,$ which means\n\n$$\n-{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-1+2=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120300 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0298e80-9e32-51b3-bea8-b2c7944b1fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477235} {:answer/id #uuid "5aa175ec-b7d6-59af-87d4-f0c15ab51cfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0298e80-9e32-51b3-bea8-b2c7944b1fa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477235} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dea1b0d-3888-5eaa-9bc2-2b09db5ea2fb" :answer-field/key "The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477587} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48c53988-eb5d-5895-afbc-11be4957b31f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477237} {:answer/id #uuid "1a08d0b2-6773-5ede-8293-415327f0bef2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477238}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a08d0b2-6773-5ede-8293-415327f0bef2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477238} :answer-field/id #uuid "32d17977-d9a7-5d42-8dfc-6d21ca476d9c" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477588} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1806f1e6-9eb0-59a6-ae69-f8bf752ad773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477239} {:answer/id #uuid "68a72fa7-84be-59ac-8cf7-064a77d59e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1806f1e6-9eb0-59a6-ae69-f8bf752ad773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477239} :answer-field/id #uuid "7619ec89-620a-5105-9e6b-579e0fa0eaa4" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477589} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce4304cc-715a-51a0-96b2-2889bb580edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668024} {:answer/id #uuid "dbd00c2e-b8e3-55ea-b3f4-974e05337696" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce4304cc-715a-51a0-96b2-2889bb580edd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668024} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4db6d8b-4a2b-5bb2-85c6-d67d77ccd910" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dd1b519a-6daa-58c6-a554-f53dcb225d1e" :question/math-academy-id "q-34153" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statements “The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$” and “The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent” are false, while statement “The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8747e1ec-5bdc-5604-985b-58468728da61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117994} {:answer/id #uuid "bf310542-d18d-58a7-8e58-a22420156a7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117995} {:answer/id #uuid "cc90ae26-d46f-5f50-bd00-0e92bd416881" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117996} {:answer/id #uuid "5599f481-dd85-552e-af10-eea6867254c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117997} {:answer/id #uuid "71e2eba5-06c7-50b6-88b0-7ea8c256dfb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117998}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "71e2eba5-06c7-50b6-88b0-7ea8c256dfb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117998} :answer-field/id #uuid "c343bbfd-7cc0-5884-946e-aa6090814a96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117993}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6f395246-75c5-52ab-b275-6f768034cd27" :question/math-academy-id "q-34243" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{3} \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5 & -1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 5 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & -3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -9\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -3\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=2 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=-3.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-3$ and from the second equation we get ${x}_{2}=3.$ Substituting these into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3+2(-3)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=11.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=11$, ${x}_{2}=3$, and ${x}_{3}=-3,$ which means \n\n$$\n11{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}-3{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=11+3-3=11.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120310 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a8765e6-0879-5856-ad1b-f5eb1d7789a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315364} {:answer/id #uuid "40775ed2-c9df-5e2a-a497-29165c069954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315488} {:answer/id #uuid "5aeb048a-16d3-59c4-b03e-ad92c8ce7998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315634} {:answer/id #uuid "862e28cf-dd10-5b90-8ece-d08261ca4a6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315869} {:answer/id #uuid "d3abbdcf-b73d-5cc1-8e30-ffe65468b6df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5aeb048a-16d3-59c4-b03e-ad92c8ce7998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315634} :answer-field/id #uuid "d7098ea9-3079-5fc0-af38-70d2a4655d4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317056}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ac599c23-1c9e-5d96-a71a-974c272cf869" :question/math-academy-id "q-34248" :question/problem "Find $x$, if $4a+6x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4a+6x & =b \\\\ 6x & =b-4a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{6}(b-4a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\begin{bmatrix}24 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}-4\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}36 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ x & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120311 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "71a2d12d-063a-5194-9872-f086deecbe0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315764} {:answer/id #uuid "b4f678bb-2e13-5906-beb2-95f91613edbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316142} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7b29bb-fb40-5f35-9053-65e121e4652d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316178} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e1a508-e59e-5b25-8a42-ad3fef836d28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316300} {:answer/id #uuid "e70bee55-c24c-5ab5-a2eb-41d32eb5308c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4f678bb-2e13-5906-beb2-95f91613edbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316142} :answer-field/id #uuid "516df2c1-bc97-57b4-8d44-e9fd43aa5d6c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4e441944-ad54-59d2-9897-793ac5452b92" :question/math-academy-id "q-34249" :question/problem "Find $l$, if $5{a}_{1}+l{a}_{2}=b$ and\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}45 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 19\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $l$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}+l{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 5\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+l\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}45 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 19\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}45 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 19\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ l\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -16\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the final equation above, we can tell that $l=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120312 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1798df1-6455-5f91-b2e6-5591c12e2277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118012} {:answer/id #uuid "dc6d4f97-9351-52f8-bee1-e1b671959955" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118013} {:answer/id #uuid "2c3aa656-e377-53ef-9901-4c3e0618b9c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118014} {:answer/id #uuid "61be6fad-5ba4-5c22-9514-ba1a6223cb34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118015} {:answer/id #uuid "7f440688-ad7a-5912-8bf3-f37679f02f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118016}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4bc05f9b-895e-594f-ad6d-4ba6fb9236e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118011}] :question/id #uuid "ad60885f-7a0b-58e2-b4e4-f60e38dd9918" :question/math-academy-id "q-34250" :question/problem "Find $q$, if $7a_{1} + qa_{2} = b$ and\n$$\n\\displaystyle a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}, a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}, b = \\begin{bmatrix}32 \\\\ 17\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120318 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fdb70cdb-77a7-57c3-b6a6-3fc0d3a96a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477241} {:answer/id #uuid "c798af58-0e1d-5b07-a685-b01936b4def8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c798af58-0e1d-5b07-a685-b01936b4def8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477242} :answer-field/id #uuid "ddfd1f41-ad17-5b57-b4ed-d56a1b4c360d" :answer-field/key "The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477590} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8244ad0a-2730-551b-82bb-26e5ff810fbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477243} {:answer/id #uuid "c86bd0e6-14a0-58a3-8204-b24c32d2ffd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c86bd0e6-14a0-58a3-8204-b24c32d2ffd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477244} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef61896-29e1-5706-91a7-6ea55283ff0f" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477591} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e01fd7c0-afad-5c3d-b6da-dc32877f541a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477245} {:answer/id #uuid "8be6cd95-0040-5363-af7f-8b2704b626e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477246}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e01fd7c0-afad-5c3d-b6da-dc32877f541a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477245} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fc6a235-aad1-5564-825b-64bf12cd21c1" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477592} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eba7fa4b-455f-59ae-9003-2d93eed75911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668026} {:answer/id #uuid "03a41de9-060e-5c57-a3e7-105df7e9a46d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eba7fa4b-455f-59ae-9003-2d93eed75911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668026} :answer-field/id #uuid "8261df59-b744-51bc-bc8b-0cd85502dc8b" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668290}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "202bc30a-b4f4-567b-8021-1d6c51e8b85e" :question/math-academy-id "q-34273" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 7{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement “The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent” is false, while statements “The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$  has an infinite number of nonzero solutions” and “The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent” are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02117761-522d-518e-9380-cd3df0b411cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563971} {:answer/id #uuid "8680a3ba-b8c5-5a4d-bba9-8c97bc9e294a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564176} {:answer/id #uuid "a4632e22-167c-5056-9f27-8ad30a2dcc0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564221} {:answer/id #uuid "d8744d9d-da34-506f-bcf4-460c113a16e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564310} {:answer/id #uuid "e97f2413-80bb-5bcf-bb04-ab19ba48bdaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8744d9d-da34-506f-bcf4-460c113a16e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564310} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5ddd77d-fd55-5b77-aa3e-054f05fd2244" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118059}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9695b9e5-18af-5741-bfa4-d11e2760dae4" :question/math-academy-id "q-34289" :question/problem "The set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n$$\n\\displaystyle {a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}=-4\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}=-4{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{a}_{1}-4{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 4{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20b6084d-45b2-5d64-9383-6b3fd0eca81c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315302} {:answer/id #uuid "6220f03a-bf7f-5f5c-888f-631b93abdb2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315670} {:answer/id #uuid "80e825ca-370b-5476-be51-4d04596db9ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-20 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315827} {:answer/id #uuid "a974e88a-3926-5177-9957-150276cc5c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316071} {:answer/id #uuid "fa3e6056-096b-5e57-a4a0-517778c31f88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a974e88a-3926-5177-9957-150276cc5c42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316071} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c7fe146-d00d-5a28-afe7-31626a5b8cda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "24ebfa1a-3835-5c3f-9168-f1537d003724" :question/math-academy-id "q-34291" :question/problem "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n$$\n\\displaystyle {a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}=5\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=5{a}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{a}_{1}-5{a}_{1} & =0 \\\\ 5{a}_{1}-{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 5{a}_{1}+(-1){a}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=5$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99d5d699-2c32-5e33-8c0a-c7bde90e4f12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = {\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118158} {:answer/id #uuid "b8b6cf7e-042b-5174-9e6f-b4eaee4e778f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = {\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118159} {:answer/id #uuid "2a3915ec-765c-578b-b7bd-2b50af4a69e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = {\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118160} {:answer/id #uuid "516a4a58-eec7-5c72-a86e-18168edd95c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = {\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118161} {:answer/id #uuid "6c4d4e39-2528-5b12-880a-f0ef64c173a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "B = {\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118162}] :answer-field/id #uuid "72c538fe-430b-5995-b3f4-aa259eaa63e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a89108a8-d6a3-5ede-8a7d-e076eed2e86f" :question/math-academy-id "q-34464" :question/problem "Consider the vectors $a_{1} = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$, $a_{2} = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$, and $a_{3} = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a basis $B$ of $Span{a_{1}, a_{2}, a_{3}}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120349 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "295ae2fa-32ce-5257-98e5-da2905531d81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317694} {:answer/id #uuid "2c0453ac-1c05-54e9-8a24-6d3978752a5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317702} {:answer/id #uuid "32214845-d636-54a9-9639-3d6949098428" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317722} {:answer/id #uuid "7f41ea8e-b9d2-5a9b-86d7-d046fada3b82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318000} {:answer/id #uuid "9e84c226-cfae-5746-8d8d-79afcdb473ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e84c226-cfae-5746-8d8d-79afcdb473ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318104} :answer-field/id #uuid "0300422c-154e-538a-8d8e-cf91e3cbdbed" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318431}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "04e10334-4152-5cfe-aad7-249b23effb61" :question/math-academy-id "q-34566" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ 6{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{3} \\\\ 9{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=-6 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3} &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9 & 7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 9 & 7\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 13\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} &=-2 \\\\ 0 &=13.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nHowever, the final equation $0=13$  gives a false statement. So the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120350 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e17edfa-489a-532b-8331-c10b33d49743" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317615} {:answer/id #uuid "5371c3dc-73f8-545d-9df1-de385114de69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317844} {:answer/id #uuid "670bbcb4-135b-58eb-8e13-6d202b4e1780" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317918} {:answer/id #uuid "7c5fdb3b-3dae-5b2c-9ba8-0af1f1050a3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317982} {:answer/id #uuid "91940bba-4486-5ef4-aa49-13aaef5d02e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c5fdb3b-3dae-5b2c-9ba8-0af1f1050a3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317982} :answer-field/id #uuid "30d08b0e-d290-5821-816b-53681a92740c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186318524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "14248ec5-b54c-565b-8b43-275a9e097f62" :question/math-academy-id "q-34568" :question/problem "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,d=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$" :question/worked-solution "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $3$ and adding the result to the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13{x}_{2} & =13\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+4(1) & =3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=1$ into the third equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =5 \\\\ 5(1)+2(1) & =5 \\\\ 7 & =5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120351 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85ac1b18-31ab-5f90-a621-3f16e7d38522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118221} {:answer/id #uuid "c938b74d-07e0-55fe-86f4-cc254226f2ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118222} {:answer/id #uuid "1297b7fd-7ca3-5efe-b2cf-8b12da9658e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118223} {:answer/id #uuid "4649fbeb-ac70-5666-a52d-deccc739449b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118224} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf0def0-c4bb-5b77-8be5-2b76998cf0c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118225}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5d2993d8-21fa-5952-974e-5bb9c99924ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118220}] :qu